                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.30017/2611.30017v1/figures/aircraft_walkthrough_render.png",
                "caption": "Figure 5:Aircraft design requires iterative engineering without access to the final product for evaluation.The agent receives a brief, a working starting design, a parts catalog and the autopilot’s code, but cannot run the simulator that grades it. For up to eight hours it iterates: measuring parts with budgeted bench tools, writing its own models of the physics, designing and checking the aircraft, and flying a few practice flights. A private simulator then flies the submitted aircraft in 34 hidden conditions. The aircraft shown is Claude Fable 5.2’s best design, the only one of 112 attempts to reach the ceiling.",
